            <ArticleTitle>Vertebral osteomyelitis secondary to Streptococcus agalactiae.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>101-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vertebral osteomyelitis due to hematogenous seeding of Streptococcus agalactiae occurred in a 29-year-old farmer. The patient was treated with immobilization and parenteral antibiotics but developed recurrent back pain requiring a posterior spinal fusion. In a review of the literature, Group B streptococcal vertebral osteomyelitis seems not to have been previously reported in an adult.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
